{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, if ndim(v_1) ≥ ndim(v_2) then ndim(v_1) − 1 else ndim(v_2) − 1] : ndim(v_1) − i − 1 < 0 ∨ ndim(v_2) − i − 1 < 0 ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) − i − 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) − i − 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) − i − 1) = shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) − i − 1)

Rule 3 (input tensors must have the same number of dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2)

Rule 10 (valid 2D transposed convolution)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : int, v_4 : int} |= ndim(v_1) = 4 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 4 ∧ v_3 ≥ 1 ∧ v_4 ≥ 0 ∧ v_3 × (shape(v_1, 2) − 1) + shape(v_2, 2) − 2 × v_4 > 0 ∧ v_3 × (shape(v_1, 3) − 1) + shape(v_2, 3) − 2 × v_4 > 0

Rule 4 (tensor data types should match)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype(v_1) = dtype(v_2)

